# Rust
src-tauri/target/
# Tauri's mobile scaffolding. Only the iOS tree is ignored wholesale;
# gen/android is TRACKED so CI can build the real Gradle project instead of
# regenerating a lookalike. The nested .gitignore files Tauri writes inside
# gen/android already exclude the right things — build output, .gradle,
# local.properties, and crucially keystore.properties / *.jks.
src-tauri/gen/apple/
src-tauri/gen/*.tmp
# Capability schemas are regenerated by tauri-build on every compile;
# tracking them just makes the working tree permanently dirty.
src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Android signing material. Tauri's own gen/android/.gitignore covers
# keystore.properties but NOT the keystore itself — staging gen/android
# picked up klaxon-release.jks on the first attempt. On a public repo that
# is a key disclosure, and Android cannot update an app across a key
# change, so a leaked-and-rotated key means every device reinstalls.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# Stray Android build output left behind by tauri-mobile when copying
# the freshly-linked .so binaries.
src-tauri/lib/

# Database
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

dev-launch.err
dev-launch.out

